  "notes": [
    "Post-route worst setup path (6_finish.rpt, report_checks -path_delay max): p_mag[1] flop -> g_mag[32] flop, data arrival 35.97 ns against 46.76 ns required, slack +10.79 ns; register to register through the AM-E1 group alignment (product magnitude, leading-one detect and shift, group magnitude), 145 data-path cells, mostly a21oi/o21ai, nor2b/nand2b and half adders. The previous record's limiter -- cfg_block_b[13] (input port) -> t_rd_addr[31] flop through the scale_index() divider, 989 cells, 97.57 ns arrival against 28.90 ns required, slack -68.67 ns -- no longer exists: the divider left the lane in 7a01ce5.",
    "Target choice: 46.0 ns is 1.106x the pre-layout search minimum of 41.575 ns in this record's fmax_search (the standalone synth,sta search of the same commit beside this record, prelayout_item11_L3.json, bisects from 40 ns to 41.60 ns). Post-route fmax 28.40 MHz (35.21 ns) is 0.847x that pre-layout minimum -- the ORFS synthesis and timing repair beat the characterization netlist, so the routing margin went unused: setup WNS +10.79 ns, hold WNS +0.396 ns. The previous record (run at 0e4222e, with the divider) had a pre-layout minimum of 62.5 ns and missed its 28 ns target by 68.67 ns.",
    "Companion probes, not committed: the same lane bytes at 7a01ce5 (rtl/ is unchanged between 7a01ce5 and 2f6b0a4; rtl/abi3/ot_a3_lane_pipelined.sv is sha256 35261aff... in both this record and the asap7 record) were routed from the earlier pinned worktree at 38, 42, 48, 56 and 64 ns: 38 ns failed pre-layout (setup WNS -3.56 ns), 42 ns passed pre-layout by +0.44 ns and closed post-route, 48, 56 and 64 ns closed, post-route fmax 27.9-28.8 MHz and 35,680-35,707 cells in every case. Those probes cite the previous lane's campaign as MAC-rate evidence and stay in scratch; this 46 ns record on 2f6b0a4 is the one kept.",
    "mac_rate_evidence sha256s are those of results/rtl/abi3_pipelined_lane.json and abi3_pipelined_lane_groups.json as committed at 2f6b0a4: the D1 and groups campaigns re-run on the divider-free lane 7a01ce5 from a clean pinned worktree on both simulators (status pass, bit_identity.equal true, measured.mac_per_lane_cycle 1.0, failure_modes.all_distinct true). The previous sky130hd record cited the campaigns of the lane before the divider was removed.",
    "Against the previous sky130hd record (a548ca2, kept beside this one as pnr_prev_a548ca2.json): cells 70,871 -> 35,724 (-49.6%), standard-cell area 486,077 -> 243,582 um2 (-49.9%), post-route fmax 10.34 -> 28.40 MHz (2.75x), pre-layout search minimum 62.5 -> 41.6 ns; not closed at 28 ns -> closed at 46 ns with DRC 0 and antenna 0."
